<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zhengdong Province</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1280–<a href="/years/1356">1356</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Branch Secretariat for the Eastern Campaign</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zhengdong Province, the Branch Secretariat for the Eastern Campaign, was an office set up by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuan-dynasty">Yuan dynasty</a> in Goryeo in 1280 to prepare the invasion of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>. It was kept after the campaign as an instrument of Yuan supervision, with the Goryeo king nominally at its head. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gongmin-of-goryeo">King Gongmin</a> dismantled its apparatus when he broke with the Yuan in 1356.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zhengdong-province.jpg" alt="Zhengdong Province" width="320" height="309" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ian Kiu; derivative work by Idh0854 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yuen_Dynasty_1294_-_Goryeo_as_vassal.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
